{
  "id": "pokepark-2005",
  "name": "PokéPark 2005",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "PokéPark was a Pokémon amusement park in Nagoya, at the Sasashima satellite site of the 2005 World Expo, open from 18 March to 25 September 2005. Entry was free, but each attraction was paid for and handed out a card of its own in a clear sealed pack, carrying the attraction's logo beside the park's: 038 to 050/PCG-P for the twelve rides the park opened with and a 3D film shown at the cinema next door, and 093/PCG-P Aura's Lucario for a walk-through added on 19 June for the film Lucario and the Mystery of Mew.\n\nThe rides ranged from the Pokémon Giant Ferris Wheel, the park's landmark, to Mudkip's Splash Adventure, a log ride. The most popular was the Pokémon Exciting Safari, where visitors caught Pokémon with a Safari Ball; on 30 April 2005 its queue reached eight hours. The park announced about 4.15 million visits, and in the summer of 2006 it moved to Taipei.",
